{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1554827732,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MzEwNjQyMTE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3311","origin":"github"},"title":"status() needs better caching","message":"ATM caching is only done inside the command for the runtime of the command. That clearly does not give the performance gains that could be achieved. With `status()` being a common first step it is worth making this as fast as anyhow possible.\n\n@kyleam do you have pointers on how `git status` caches its results?\n\n I think caches would be placed in the top-level dataset only and for any subdataset of any depth. Likely caches could *not* be put into each dataset in a hierachy, because doing so would invalidate the `mtime` of their root directory -- which is the only thing that I can think of that would help with status-speedup in the face of untracked/uncommitted changes.","files":null}]}